//! Use cases: orchestration, and nothing else.
//!
//! Each method does the same few things — load, call the domain, save, publish what the
//! domain raised — and most of that is one call: `Store::change` loads the aggregate,
//! applies a domain method, and saves it with a version check. The business rules
//! themselves are one ring in, in `domain/`. If a rule starts being written *here*, it
//! has leaked out of the hexagon.
//!
//! A use case is a method on a plain struct that holds its ports. There is no trait to
//! implement; `#[jenny::use_cases]` on the `impl` block gives every method a span and a
//! duration measurement, and generates nothing else.
